{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794555010,"nonce":"+2FpU4StjdAB7bqHhwF/BbbQ15Y=","message":"Feasibility spike, 2026-11-13, iOS simulator (aarch64-apple-ios-sim, Xcode SDK, no other setup). The program ran; what is missing is tooling, not the runtime.\n\nWorks:\n- The runtime builds for the target (libash_std.a, 35.9 MB), but only with `BINDGEN_EXTRA_CLANG_ARGS_aarch64_apple_ios_sim` pointing at the SDK sysroot; std/build.rs finds no headers on its own.\n- `ash --build --target aarch64-apple-ios-sim` writes the AOT object.\n- Linked by hand with `xcrun --sdk iphonesimulator clang` and `-framework CoreFoundation` (5.2 MB executable), then run under `xcrun simctl spawn` on a booted simulator: hello world and ten test programs print what the interpreter prints, exit 0.\n\nGaps, each a step of this issue's acceptance list:\n- Item 2: header discovery needs the env var above.\n- Item 4: `ash --build` stops with \"native executable linking is not configured for aarch64-apple-ios-sim\"; there is no link step and nothing that adds CoreFoundation.\n- Item 3: the object carries no platform tag. Device and simulator objects are byte-identical, so ld warns and assumes.\n- The deliverable decided in comment #2 is a static archive for the app's `main`; the spike linked an executable, so the archive path and the entry glue are untried.\n\nNot tested: threads and fibers, GC under memory pressure, a physical device, HDLL natives (no static binding path yet), x86_64 simulator.","files":null}]}